<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Reading a cumulative frequency table</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The table shows the cumulative frequencies of the masses, in kg (to the nearest kg), of \({@n@}\) sacks of potatoes at Nyahururu market.</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Mass (kg)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[1]@}–{@hi[1]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[2]@}–{@hi[2]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[3]@}–{@hi[3]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[4]@}–{@hi[4]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[5]@}–{@hi[5]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[6]@}–{@hi[6]@}</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Cumulative frequency (cf)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[6]@}</td></tr></table><p>(a) How many sacks weigh less than \({@exd(ucb[k])@}\) kg?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) How many sacks weigh \({@exd(ucb[j])@}\) kg or more?</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) How many sacks are in the class {@lo[m]@}–{@hi[m]@}?</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The cumulative frequency at an upper class boundary counts every value below that boundary. So the cumulative frequency of a class counts every sack in that class and in all the classes before it.</p><p>(a) \({@exd(ucb[k])@}\) kg is the upper class boundary of {@lo[k]@}–{@hi[k]@}, so \({@cf[k]@}\) sacks weigh less than it.</p><p>(b) \({@cf[j]@}\) sacks weigh less than \({@exd(ucb[j])@}\) kg, so \({@n@} - {@cf[j]@} = {@ta2@}\) weigh \({@exd(ucb[j])@}\) kg or more.</p><p>(c) Subtract the cumulative frequency of the class before: \({@cf[m]@} - {@cf[m-1]@} = {@ta3@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
